+- GDN switch: a new run-time switch of this design. It turns the GDN block path of Part A off alone.
+- token path, column-half path, block path: the three code paths of the GDN recurrence. Token path: step() per token, today's code. Column-half path: advance() with the loop order of Part 0. Block path: advance() with the block kernel of Part A.
+- session: one series of runs on delphi-3b35 without a reboot and without a change of the server's own settings (CPU settings, SYSTEM_CONFIG) between them.
 - cell: one combination of user count and prompt length.
 - prompt N: a prompt of N tokens. Every baseline run then generates 256 tokens per user. A traced run generates 32 tokens per user.
 - Part 0, Part A, Part B: the three proposed changes. Part 0: a new loop order for GDN prompt processing, without AMX. Part A: the AMX block kernel for GDN. Part B: the AMX attention kernel for 256-wide heads.
