+- In a GDN layer the FPGA projections, the host work and the next projection run one after another. So a time saved in GDN shortens the pass by the same amount.
+- In an attention layer the scoring of the full pages starts when Q is ready. It can run while the FPGA cards produce K and V of the pass [Ref8]. Assumption of the model: with Part B on, this scoring still ends after K and V are ready. Under this assumption a time saved in attention shortens the pass by the same amount. The open point on the wait for K and V names the measurement that tests it.
 
